── GATE SWEEP (loosen each gate one notch -> fwd return of the names it NEWLY admits) ──
  positive = the gate was too tight (newly-admitted beat the field); ≤0 = it's keeping junk out.
  the TOO TIGHT flag needs mean AND median positive — one survivor can carry a mean on its own.
  vs shipped = newly-admitted median MINUS the accepted cohort's median (-119.5); >0 = no worse than what the gates already keep.
